%% Kaur Khor desktop navigation benchmark architecture.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Bench as Navigation benchmark<br/>bench/scenarios/navigation.bench.ts
  participant Shell as KaurKhorShell sidebar
  participant Router as React Router<br/>BenchmarkRouteObserver
  participant Provider as InventoryProvider<br/>PreferencesProvider
  participant Route as Route components
  participant Preload as Preload bridge<br/>window.kaurKhorDesktop
  participant Main as Electron main IPC<br/>benchmarkIpcHandle
  participant Core as Managed desktop-core pool
  participant Store as SQLite read models<br/>and checkpoints
  participant Metrics as Benchmark summary<br/>bench/helpers/bench-metrics.ts

  Bench->>Provider: wait for renderer.workspace.ready
  Bench->>Shell: click visible sidebar item
  Shell->>Router: update hash route
  Router->>Metrics: record renderer.route.navigation start
  Router->>Route: load lazy route chunk
  Route->>Provider: read hot inventory and preference state

  alt route needs support data
    Route->>Preload: sena or automation read
    Preload->>Metrics: record preload.invoke.* span
    Preload->>Main: IPC command
    Main->>Main: check SENA read cache
    alt cache hit
      Main-->>Preload: cached response
    else cache miss or stale fingerprint
      Main->>Core: coalesced read-only command
      Core->>Store: read hot rows, detail rows, or paged rows
      Store-->>Core: response rows
      Core-->>Main: backend.core.response.received
      Main-->>Preload: response
    end
    Preload-->>Route: data
  else route is already hydrated
    Route->>Route: render from provider state
  end

  Route->>Router: markRouteReady when route surface is stable
  Router->>Metrics: record route.*.ready and memory snapshot
  Bench->>Metrics: record nav.* duration
  Bench->>Shell: continue route loop

  Bench->>Shell: open Settings, then Back to app
  Shell->>Router: restore originating app route from navigation state
  Router->>Metrics: wait route.insights.explain.ready
  Bench->>Route: open recent receipt task drawer
  Route->>Metrics: record interaction.open_task_drawer_ms
  Bench->>Metrics: close app and persist navigation.summary.json

  Note over Router,Route: Ready events wait for preferences, inventory loading, and route-specific stable UI.
  Note over Shell,Router: Settings carries the prior app location so Back to app returns to that route instead of Home.
  Note over Main,Core: Identical read-only commands are globally coalesced before worker selection.
  Note over Store: Navigation should use route-scoped reads, not startup-wide observation hydration.
